763	     * one identified by {@code excludeId} (pass {@code null} to consider every owner, e.g. on
764	     * create). The key is derived in one place — {@link OwnerMapper#toIdentityKey(Owner)}, the same
765	     * method that builds the {@code identityKey} returned on the DTO — so the value governing the
766	     * 409 is exactly the value clients see. Only an exact full-key match counts as a duplicate.
767	     *
768	     * @param identityKey the identity key to look for
769	     * @param excludeId   id of an owner to ignore during the check, or {@code null} for none
770	     * @return {@code true} if another owner already has the same identity key
771	     */
