184	    /**
185	     * Format an owner's stored E.164 {@code telephone} for humans: the country code, a space, then the
186	     * national digits grouped in threes (e.g. {@code "+61412345678"} becomes {@code "+61 412 345 678"}).
187	     * The raw {@code telephone} property is left untouched in E.164 form. Returns the value unchanged
188	     * when it is {@code null} or not in {@code '+'}-prefixed E.164 form.
189	     *
