summary:
I now have the complete picture. Here is the full, ordered code path for creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`.

---

## Overview of the execution order

1. Spring Security filter chain authorizes the request
2. `OwnersApi.addOwner` (generated interface default → overridden) receives the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` — Bean Validation runs here
3. `@PreAuthorize` method-security check on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`
4. `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` runs all business logic / side effects
5. `OwnerMapper` maps DTO→entity and (later) entity→DTO
6. `ClinicServiceImpl` methods → `OwnerRepository`
7. On any thrown `ResponseStatusException` etc., `ExceptionControllerAdvice` builds the error response

Note: **there are no JPA `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate` callbacks, no `@EntityListeners`, and no `ApplicationEventListener`s** anywhere in this path — the "event" is a plain immutable record logged to SLF4J, not a Spring `ApplicationEvent`. The only custom `ConstraintValidator` in the project (`PetAgeValidator`) applies to **Pet** birthDate, **not** Owner, so it is not on this path.

---

## 1. Security config affecting the endpoint

Two mutually-exclusive configs selected by the `petclinic.security.enable` property.

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java` (active when `=true`):
- Line 19: `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)` — this is what makes the controller's `@PreAuthorize` effective.
- Lines 34-43: filter chain — CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().authenticated()`, HTTP Basic.
- Lines 27-29: `BCryptPasswordEncoder` bean (used for user auth, not owner creation).
- Lines 46-53: JDBC authentication wiring.

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java` (active when `=false`): lines 20-32 permit all requests.

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java` line 8: `public final String OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN";` — referenced by SpEL `@roles.OWNER_ADMIN`.

---

## 2. The @RestController method

`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration (lines 65-68):
```java
@RestController
@CrossOrigin(exposedHeaders = "errors, content-type")
@RequestMapping("/api")
public class OwnerRestControllerV1 implements OwnersApi {
```

The HTTP mapping, `@Valid` and `@RequestBody` live on the **generated interface** `OwnersApi` (see section below). The controller overrides the method (lines 140-215):

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    String idempotencyKey = this.request.getHeader(IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_HEADER);
    Integer existingId = this.idempotencyKeyRegistry.findOwnerId(idempotencyKey);
    if (existingId != null) {
        Owner existing = this.clinicService.findOwnerById(existingId);
        if (existing != null) {
            return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(existing), HttpStatus.OK);
        }
    }
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    String normalizedTelephone = normalizeTelephone(owner.getTelephone());
    owner.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
    owner.setEmail(normalizeEmail(owner.getEmail()));
    applyAddress(owner);
    validatePostcode(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode());
    LocalDate effectiveRegistrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
    if (effectiveRegistrationDate == null) {
        effectiveRegistrationDate = LocalDate.now();
    } else if (effectiveRegistrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST,
            "registrationDate must not be later than the current server date");
    }
    effectiveRegistrationDate = rollToBusinessDay(effectiveRegistrationDate);
    owner.setRegistrationDate(effectiveRegistrationDate);
    if (countOwnersRegisteredOn(effectiveRegistrationDate) >= DAILY_CREATE_LIMIT) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS,
            "the maximum number of owners that may be created today has been reached");
    }
    boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
    this.clinicService.assignHousehold(owner);
    boolean householdInUse = this.clinicService.isHouseholdInUse(owner.getHouseholdId(), null);
    if (isIdentityKeyInUse(ownerMapper.toIdentityKey(owner), null)) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
            "an owner with the same identity already exists");
    }
    int ownersInCity = countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity());
    if (ownersInCity >= CITY_CAPACITY) {
        throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT,
            "city has reached its maximum number of owners");
    }
    owner.setCapacityWarning(ownersInCity >= CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD);
    owner.setMemberId(memberIdFor(owner));
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
    owner.setHouseholdSize(countHouseholdMembers(owner.getHouseholdId()) + 1);
    owner.setMembershipLevelCap(householdMembershipLevelCap(owner.getHouseholdId()));
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(
        countOwnersRegisteredOn(effectiveRegistrationDate) > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD);
    boolean declaredHouseholdMember = sharesHousehold && householdInUse;
    Owner softDuplicate = declaredHouseholdMember ? null : findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicate(softDuplicate != null);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(softDuplicate == null ? null : softDuplicate.getId());
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    this.idempotencyKeyRegistry.record(idempotencyKey, owner.getId());
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    AUDIT.info("owner created: id={} memberId={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
        ownerDto.getMembershipLevel());
    OwnerCreatedEvent event = OwnerCreatedEvent.of(AUDIT_EVENT_SEQUENCE.incrementAndGet(),
        owner.getId(), primaryIdentifier(owner), ownerDto.getOwnerSegment(),
